;; the revision clojure/ was seeded from. Run on OpenJDK 26.0.2.1, direct linking on (upstream's
;; default), each namespace in its own JVM after requiring all test namespaces.
;;
;; :namespaces maps each test namespace to its clojure.test counts: :test deftests run, :pass,
;; :fail and :error assertions, and for failing deftests their :fail/:error counts. A namespace
;; that fails to load has :load-error. The counts are stable from run to run.
;;
;; Control run: the same script on upstream's own build of that revision (src/jvm with its bundled
;; ASM, src/clj, spec.alpha 0.6.249, core.specs.alpha 0.6.133-alpha10) on the same JDK gives
;; 83 namespaces, 809 tests, 20750 assertions, all passing, and 27 test.generative specs, all
;; passing. So nothing below is caused by the environment (JDK 26, locale, network, timing) or by
;; a missing test library: every difference comes from the stubbed spec or is a baseline bug.
